and discards the draft; counting follows FR-022 regardless of whether the abort succeeds. Before returning a draft, 
the server rechecks that the caller is still a member of the note's company and the note still exists; otherwise the 
draft is discarded. | Must | AC-016, AC-030 |
 123: | FR-022 | Usage: each provider dispatch counts toward the company's daily limit, whether it succeeds, times 
out, returns unusable output, or the user leaves. A dispatch is refunded only when the provider's documented protocol 
signals rejection before processing — an HTTP authentication/permission error, or a rate-limit/overload/unavailable 
HTTP error status returned before any response body or stream event — as defined per adapter in the capability matrix; 
every other or ambiguous outcome stays counted. Not counted at all: files rejected by FR-013, inputs refused by 
FR-020, failures before dispatch. Admission atomically reserves one unit against the limit before dispatch; concurrent 
requests cannot exceed the limit; each reservation covers exactly one dispatch and settles at most once against the 
day of its admission; a reservation without a recorded outcome (server crash) stays counted; only server code settles 
reservations — no client role can classify, refund, or alter usage. | Must | AC-016, AC-028, AC-029 |
 124: | FR-023 | When the company's count for the current day (midnight to midnight, America/Sao_Paulo) has reached 
its limit, processing is refused with a message stating the limit and the reset time. | Must | AC-016 |
