way. Deleting a user keeps the notes, versions, and name snapshots (the live reference becomes empty); it never blocks 
the deletion or deletes company notes. | Must | AC-020, AC-023, AC-031 |
 131: | FR-030 | Participants and assignees are stored by application `users.id` with a display-name snapshot. A 
person who is no longer a member of the note's company (company changed, removed, or user deleted) is shown as "Former 
member" (with the snapshot name), keeps their place in the note and its versions, and has no access. If the same 
`users.id` becomes a member of the same company again, their author/participant/assignee rights return. New selections 
accept current members only; saving or restoring may retain former members already present. | Must | AC-021 |
 132: | FR-031 | Every processing start carries an idempotency key scoped to the authenticated application user, 
company, and operation, and bound to the note id, source note revision, transcript identity, and settings revision. A 
replay with the same key and binding returns the same pending or final result without a new dispatch (after 
re-authorizing the caller); a replay with a different binding is rejected; keys are kept for at least 48 hours, across 
midnight, so a delayed replay never counts again. "Try again" after a failure is a new operation with a new key and a 
new admission. | Must | AC-028 |
