 283: ## 15. Test strategy
 284: 
 285: - Levels: integration and E2E only (AGENTS.md). No unit tests; no mocking of Supabase, repositories, or the code 
under test.
 286: - Integration (Vitest against local Supabase and real API routes): RLS and route authorization per role and 
company, including direct-client attacks (AC-004, AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-017, AC-021, AC-023, AC-024); validation 
limits (AC-002, AC-009, AC-011); revisions and conflicts with competing transactions (AC-005); versions (AC-006); 
transcript normalization (AC-012); assignee matching (AC-013); usage counting, reservations, idempotency, reset 
(AC-016, AC-028); settings revision binding (AC-025); outbound retries, refund classification, idempotency binding and 
replay, in-flight membership removal, draft source revision, user deletion (AC-028, AC-029, AC-030, AC-031); adapters 
and preflight (AC-026); reprocess merge (AC-027); search fields, languages, ordering, pagination, isolation, and 
timing with 1,000 seeded notes (AC-014); space and company deletion (AC-020); key canary (AC-017).
 287: - External AI provider: replaced in automated tests only, by a local fake server speaking each provider's API, 
selected by environment configuration, recording received requests, with fixed responses and scripted failures (error 
after processing, timeout, refusal, malformed JSON, auth rejection, unavailable). Database, RLS, routes, and UI stay 
real.
 288: - E2E (Playwright, two accounts): manual note lifecycle, rendering and sanitization, editing rights, conflict, 
history/restore, action items with assignee completion, transcript upload → review → Apply, reprocess, AI-disabled 
state, admin settings, search, export download, dashboard link (AC-001, AC-003–AC-008, AC-010, AC-015, AC-018, AC-019, 
AC-027).
 289: - Test data: fictional transcripts in .txt/.vtt/.srt, Portuguese and English, including speaker names, accents, 
a one-hour fixture, and malformed files. No real personal data.
 290: - Cadence: per task type-check + lint; per block type-check, lint, DB integration suite when server code 
changed; one final Chrome-only E2E run of all new specs plus the full regression suite, zero retries; one test process 
at a time.
 291: - Owner test: AC-022 with a real OpenAI key against the online database after the migrations are applied.
