  23: **Section B: New findings**
  24: 
  25: 1. **High — N1 — FR-022, §9: SDK retries escape the reservation.**
  26: 
  27:    **Problem/scenario:** A provider accepts processing, but the connection fails before the response arrives. 
The official SDK retries, producing additional potentially billable dispatches under one reservation. Start-request 
idempotency does not constrain these outbound retries. OpenAI and Anthropic document automatic retries by default. 
[OpenAI Docs](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript#retries), [Anthropic error 
documentation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/errors).
  28: 
  29:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:123](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:123), 
[SPEC:166](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:166).  
  30:    **SPEC fix:** Disable transparent SDK/transport retries. Every additional provider dispatch requires separate 
admission/accounting. Test connection loss after provider acceptance through real routes and DB, asserting the fake 
server’s received-request count.
  31: 
  32: 2. **Medium — N2 — FR-022, AC-016: “rejected without processing” lacks an observable classification contract.**
  33: 
  34:    **Problem/scenario:** An overload error can occur after an accepted streaming response. Refunding every 
“overloaded/unavailable” error would refund processed work. A fake server’s internal knowledge that processing 
happened cannot establish what the application can infer from the real provider protocol. [Anthropic streaming 
errors](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming#error-events).
  35: 
  36:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:123](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:123), 
[SPEC:261](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:261), 
[SPEC:279](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:279).  
  37:    **SPEC fix:** Define provider-specific, documented pre-processing rejection signals. Ambiguous outcomes 
remain counted. Clients cannot classify or refund attempts, including through RPCs. Settlement releases a reservation 
at most once against its original day. Tests must use observable production protocol signals, without private 
“processed” flags.
  38: 
  39: 3. **Medium — N3 — FR-022, AC-028: idempotency keys have no scope, payload binding, or lifetime.**
  40: 
  41:    **Problem/scenario:** A client reuses a key for another note or changed transcript; two callers collide; or a 
delayed retry crosses midnight and a company/day lookup treats it as new. The SPEC does not define mismatch responses, 
pending/terminal replay behavior, or retention.
  42: 
  43:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:123](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:123), 
[SPEC:172](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:172), 
[SPEC:273](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:273).  
  44:    **SPEC fix:** Scope keys to authenticated company, application user, and operation; bind them to 
note/input/settings revisions. Reject changed payloads. Define replay retention across midnight and crash recovery, 
reauthorize every replay, and distinguish transport retry from a deliberate new “Try again” operation.
  45: 
  46: 4. **Medium — N4 — FR-030, BR-001: removal during generation has no response-time authorization gate.**
  47: 
  48:    **Problem/scenario:** A member starts generation, an admin removes them while the provider is processing, and 
the pending response delivers company-derived content after removal. Dispatch-time authorization and database RLS do 
not protect that provider response.
  49: 
  50:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:117](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:117), 
[SPEC:131](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:131); membership removal clears 
company affiliation at [migration:770](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260718210827_phase7_company_mem
ber_atomic_removal.sql:770).  
  51:    **SPEC fix:** Recheck current membership and note existence before returning a draft; recheck mutation rights 
inside Apply’s transaction. Discard pending UI results on membership-scope changes. Add a paused-provider test with 
real member removal.
  52: 
  53: 5. **Medium — N5 — FR-007, FR-016, FR-018: the draft’s source revision is unspecified.**
  54: 
  55:    **Problem/scenario:** Generation starts from transcript T1. Another editor uploads T2; the first browser 
refreshes to the latest note revision. Apply can submit that latest revision with the old T1 draft, passing revision 
comparison while applying stale material.
  56: 
  57:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:108](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:108), 
[SPEC:117](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:117), 
[SPEC:119](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:119).  
  58:    **SPEC fix:** Snapshot the stored transcript and note revision at generation start; carry that source 
revision with the draft. Apply compares against that revision, even after UI refreshes. Test replacement while the 
fake provider is paused.
  59: 
  60: 6. **Medium — N6 — FR-015/016, §12: v2 adds undisclosed roster export.**
  61: 
  62:    **Problem/scenario:** Processing an unrelated meeting sends every current employee’s display name to the 
provider. The recorded answer and privacy notice describe sending transcript text, so members whose names are absent 
from the transcript are nevertheless exported.
  63: 
  64:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:117](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:117), 
[SPEC:233](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:233), [owner 
answer:63](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:63).  
  65:    **SPEC fix:** Extract suggested names from the transcript and resolve them against company members locally. A 
full-roster transfer requires a separate owner decision and explicit disclosure in the notice.
  66: 
  67: 7. **Medium — N7 — FR-008/029/030, §9: deleted authors and version editors lack a durable lifecycle contract.**
  68: 
  69:    **Problem/scenario:** An author or historical editor is deleted. The new creator reference has no deletion 
rule, and snapshots cover participants/assignees only. Ordinary FK choices can block deletion, delete company notes, 
or erase historical attribution.
  70: 
  71:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:109](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:109), 
[SPEC:131](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:131), 
[SPEC:171](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:171); existing editor FK uses SET 
NULL at [baseline:1401](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:1401).  
  72:    **SPEC fix:** Preserve immutable author/editor UUID and name snapshots independently of nullable live-user 
references. User deletion must preserve notes and immutable history. Define rejoin rights by stable application 
identity and test author/editor deletion.
  73: 
  74: 8. **Low — N8 — FR-021, scope: navigation cancellation was weakened without an owner decision.**
  75: 
  76:    **Problem/scenario:** A user leaves, but processing continues because v2 requires only draft discard. Round 4 
changed counting; it did not revoke the earlier cancellation decision.
  77: 
  78:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:80](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:80), 
[SPEC:122](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:122), [owner 
answers:91](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:91), [round 
4:122](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:122).  
  79:    **SPEC fix:** Require cancellation of the browser request and best-effort abortion of the outbound request, 
while retaining post-dispatch counting regardless of provider cancellation success.
  80: 
  81: 9. **Low — N9 — AC-009: the capacity fixture masks other validators.**
  82: 
  83:    **Problem/scenario:** With 100 existing items, every attempted insertion fails on capacity—even if 
description length and assignee eligibility are never validated. The acceptance test can therefore pass with those 
guards missing.
  84: 
  85:    **Evidence:** [SPEC:254](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:254).  
  86:    **SPEC fix:** Use a below-capacity fixture for invalid descriptions and former/cross-company assignees. 
Reserve the 100-item fixture for capacity assertions.
