 ## 15. Test strategy
 
 - Levels: integration and E2E only (AGENTS.md). No unit tests; no mocking of Supabase, repositories, or the code 
under test.
-- Integration (Vitest against local Supabase): RLS and route authorization per role and company (AC-004, AC-007, 
AC-008, AC-017, AC-021, AC-023); validation limits (AC-002, AC-009, AC-011); version creation and conflict (AC-005, 
AC-006); transcript normalization (AC-012); assignee matching (AC-013); limit counting and failure non-counting 
(AC-016); search correctness, isolation, and timing with 1,000 seeded notes (AC-014); space deletion (AC-020); key 
never returned (AC-017).
-- External AI provider: replaced in automated tests only, by a local fake server speaking the provider APIs, selected 
by environment configuration, with fixed responses and scripted failures (error, timeout, refusal, invalid key). 
Database, RLS, routes, and UI stay real.
-- E2E (Playwright, two accounts): manual note lifecycle, editing rights, conflict, history/restore, action items with 
assignee completion, transcript → review → save, AI-disabled state, admin settings, search, export download, 
sanitization (AC-001, AC-003–AC-008, AC-010, AC-015, AC-018, AC-019).
-- Test data: fictional transcripts in .txt/.vtt/.srt, Portuguese and English, including speaker names, accents, and 
malformed files. No real personal data.
+- Integration (Vitest against local Supabase and real API routes): RLS and route authorization per role and company, 
including direct-client attacks (AC-004, AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-017, AC-021, AC-023, AC-024); validation limits 
(AC-002, AC-009, AC-011); revisions and conflicts with competing transactions (AC-005); versions (AC-006); transcript 
normalization (AC-012); assignee matching (AC-013); usage counting, reservations, idempotency, reset (AC-016, AC-028); 
settings revision binding (AC-025); adapters and preflight (AC-026); reprocess merge (AC-027); search fields, 
languages, ordering, pagination, isolation, and timing with 1,000 seeded notes (AC-014); space and company deletion 
(AC-020); key canary (AC-017).
+- External AI provider: replaced in automated tests only, by a local fake server speaking each provider's API, 
selected by environment configuration, recording received requests, with fixed responses and scripted failures (error 
after processing, timeout, refusal, malformed JSON, auth rejection, unavailable). Database, RLS, routes, and UI stay 
real.
+- E2E (Playwright, two accounts): manual note lifecycle, rendering and sanitization, editing rights, conflict, 
history/restore, action items with assignee completion, transcript upload → review → Apply, reprocess, AI-disabled 
state, admin settings, search, export download, dashboard link (AC-001, AC-003–AC-008, AC-010, AC-015, AC-018, AC-019, 
AC-027).
+- Test data: fictional transcripts in .txt/.vtt/.srt, Portuguese and English, including speaker names, accents, a 
one-hour fixture, and malformed files. No real personal data.
 - Cadence: per task type-check + lint; per block type-check, lint, DB integration suite when server code changed; one 
final Chrome-only E2E run of all new specs plus the full regression suite, zero retries; one test process at a time.
-- Owner test: AC-022 with a real provider key against the online database after the migrations are applied.
+- Owner test: AC-022 with a real OpenAI key against the online database after the migrations are applied.
 
